WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.100
The mushrooms said, and I'm sure you'll be horrified of this,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.440
the mushroom said to me in the Amazon,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.360
when they were revealing all this information

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.080
and deputizing us to do all these things

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.420
we said, "Why us?"

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:02.160
"Why should WE be," you know, "the ambassador of an alien species into human culture?"

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.760
and they said, "Because you have never believed anybody."

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.980
"Because you have never given over your belief to anyone."

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:06.580
Uh, in 1971, I was 23, my brother was 19

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.660
I spent several years in Asia already

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.680
having been run out of Berkeley

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.680
because of the revolution

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.320
and, uh, we

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.320
were

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.360
graduates of the LSD revolution

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.860
but it had left us wanting more

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.720
specifically, wanting the kinds of experiences

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.520
that the classical commentators on psychedelics described

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.720
and by that I mean people like Havelock Ellis in The Dance Of Life

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.160
or, uh,  S. Weir Mitchell

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.020
who wrote about mescaline

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.980
LSD, for us, never delivered

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.420
uh, visions

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:57.200
it delivered insight and feelings and complex thoughts

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.200
but not visions

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.520
not activity in the visual cortex

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.320
that these classical commentators had led us to expect

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.380
and I had been in India for a number of years

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.900
and pretty well managed to convince myself

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.100
that whatever spirituality had ever been there

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.580
it had evaporated thousands of years ago

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.480
and that what we were left with was a very

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.780
grasping and mendacious priestly hierarchy

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.360
that was about as cynical as religion gets

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.000
and I was raised Catholic so I know what I'm talking about

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:43.560
and, uh, so then we decided: well, where the gnosis must be, is in the Amazon

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:50.680
where we knew there was a pristine, aboriginal shamanism based on hallucinogens

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.520
and I stress our youth

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.300
because, I think, people imagine

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:04.300
that you can only make contributions if you're old and ladened with degrees

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.180
and that sort of thing

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.380
and basically, our pure, reckless inventiveness

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:18.520
carried us further into the heart of the Mystery than I would have ever believed possible

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:23.880
and I should say a little bit about the method because I think it's important:

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.880
um..

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:32.180
rationalism in confrontation with the weird edges

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.960
is what's always worked for me

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:40.580
in other words, if you're a true believer, if you have some pre-packaged philosophy

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.360
then you're going to miss a great deal

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:49.360
because you're pre-programmed to ignore what doesn't fit into your model

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.400
and it doesn't matter what your model is

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.800
uh, but if you're simply

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:00.960
the open minded sceptic / witness

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.780
and then, if you push at the edges of the phenomenal world

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.460
you know, go to the highest mountains

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.600
the oldest cities

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.340
the deepest deserts

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.800
the most remote jungles

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.960
and just simply put yourself in these circumstances,

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.920
the cosmic giggle can get at you

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:32.500
you know, it can't get at you if you're pursuing your job delivering messages for Matthew and Son

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.620
or whatever it is you've got going

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:39.460
but if you will tear the human atom of your individuality

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.380
out of the collectivity

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:47.080
and set yourself into a wilderness, a desert, an uninhabited island

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:52.080
then this thing can rise out of the depths

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:56.680
and communicate if it chooses, shape your life, for sure

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:58.360
blow your mind

